{
  "about": "Second catalog for tests/compat/run.sh (--catalog). Mostly apps with no Flathub listing at all, official or unofficial, so that debpak's conversion is the only way to get a Flatpak of them; about two dozen that are on Flathub stay in as reference checks. Each comes from its vendor as a Windows or macOS program, a Linux package, an AppImage, a tarball or a snap. source uses the recipe check types (github, redirect, html, json) plus url (a fixed link to the latest file) and snap (snap download). expect is runs, or refused when debpak should decline the app (system services, drivers, VPN clients, programs that only work as root). args are extra convert options; seconds is how long the app gets to start; tray marks an app that only shows a tray icon; cli a command-line tool.",
